# Copy this file to .env.local and add your own Google Maps JavaScript API key.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# The key is used ONLY for the Street View panorama. The guessing and result
# maps use Leaflet + OpenStreetMap and require no key.
#
# Restrict this browser key in Google Cloud Console:
#   - Application restriction: HTTP referrers (websites)
#       http://localhost:5173/*  (dev)
#       https://your-domain.example/*  (production)
#   - API restriction: Maps JavaScript API only
#
# NOTE: A browser API key is always visible to end users. Referrer + API
# restrictions are the correct protection — never rely on hiding it in source.
#
# The app still builds, tests, and launches without a key; it will show a
# polished setup screen explaining that Street View is unavailable.

VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# ── Private multiplayer (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Real-time 1v1 multiplayer is powered by Supabase. Solo mode works without
# these; when they are absent the multiplayer menu shows a friendly setup note
# instead of crashing. See docs/MULTIPLAYER_SETUP.md for full instructions.
#
# Use the PUBLISHABLE (browser) key ONLY — never a secret/service_role key.
# A browser key is safe to ship: Row Level Security on the database is what
# actually protects the data. Find both values in your Supabase project under
# Project Settings → API.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
